"origin":"FIREBASE_SYSTEM"},{"variable":"NG_TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS","value":"X-Forwarded-Host","availability":["RUNTIME"],"origin":"FIREBASE_SYSTEM"},{"variable":"NG_ALLOWED_HOSTS","value":"markaestro-227206788749.us-central1.run.app,markaestro-auwks5pljq-uc.a.run.app,t-2029476607---markaestro-auwks5pljq-uc.a.run.app,markaestro--markaestro-0226220726.us-central1.hosted.app","availability":["RUNTIME"],"origin":"FIREBASE_SYSTEM"}]},"source":{"codebase":{"branch":"main","displayName":"a39282492d07261d89a7e1f333be447d7fa52f33","hash":"a39282492d07261d89a7e1f333be447d7fa52f33","commitMessage":"fix(publish): stop a completed TikTok publish toasting \"tiktok: undefined\"\n\nThe publish route's inline TikTok poll updates publishResults in\nFirestore, but the response still carried the pre-poll snapshot where\nTikTok reads success:false, pending:true with no error. A Direct Post\nthat completed inside the poll window came back status:published with\nthat stale channel entry, and the composer's failure loop rendered it\nas \"tiktok: undefined\".\n\nTwo halves: the route re-reads publishResults once the poll reaches a\nterminal state, and the composer's failure toasts now come from\ngetFailedChannelResults, which excludes pending and error-less entries\nso a stale snapshot can never render as a failure again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","uri":"https://github.com/D3vBaba/Markaestro/commit/a39282492d07261d89a7e1f333be447d7fa52f33","author":{"displayName":"Rodney Sama-Ambe","email":"rodneysa@aethossolutions.com"},"commitTime":"2026-08-15T05:49:52Z"}},"buildLogsUri":"https://console.cloud.google.com/cloud-build/builds;region=us-central1/0bce3407-3e1d-4f56-a597-c7b60b1e4e32?project=227206788749","createTime":"2026-08-15T05:49:55.217261849Z","updateTime":"2026-08-15T05:55:39.401759Z","displayName":"build-2026-08-15-002","uid":"b8317061-0a10-4151-a69e-ab1890d6c971","etag":"JX_t0qns-HR1goHP33-v6kkmXc10PHZGpke0za48OF0","reconciling":false},{"name