bfa7f6bac72dd9","commitMessage":"fix(lint): clear every eslint error across the app surface\n\nThe tree had 33 errors, all pre-existing: React's newer hook rules\n(set-state-in-effect, purity) and next/no-html-link-for-pages started\nfiring once the i18n work landed. Fixed by shape, not by suppression.\n\nState that mirrors a prop or the URL is now derived during render instead\nof synced in an effect — the query cache re-seed on key change, page\nresets on brand change, the Settings tab, calendar filters from the URL,\nthe analytics range clamp, the post edit sheet's fields, and onboarding's\nregister-step advance and plan recommendation. Each of those cost an\nextra render pass and, more visibly, a frame showing the previous value.\n\nWork that genuinely is a side effect — fetching, reading localStorage,\nhandling an OAuth return — keeps its effect but starts via\ndeferFromEffect, a microtask hop so the loading flag no longer lands\nsynchronously inside the effect. It resolves before paint, so nothing\nflickers.\n\nThree reads of Date.now() during render (trial end date, trial days left,\nAPI key expiry badge) are now sampled once per mount, so a component's\noutput no longer depends on when React happened to re-render it.\n\nTen internal <a> elements became <Link>, restoring client-side navigation\non those paths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","uri":"https://github.com/D3vBaba/Markaestro/commit/726784612eabaa59316d940a3abfa7f6bac72dd9","author":{"displayName":"Rodney Sama-Ambe","email":"rodneysa@aethossolutions.com"},"commitTime":"2026-08-09T07:17:15Z"}},"buildLogsUri":"https://console.cloud.google.com/cloud-build/builds;region=us-central1/e4bb583f-3b92-48ea-9d35-8743a18ad780?project=227206788749","createTime":"2026-08-09T07:17:18.810713182Z","updateTime":"2026-08-09T07:22:42.822612Z","displayName":"build-2026-08-09-005","uid":"77ebd16a-8e0d-470b-bf6a-46e26df38f87","etag":"cGJuZVfDNiH8lQlyM91d1YkL7E3XRDD1OzBb7ZhDBXk","reco