-uc.a.run.app,markaestro--markaestro-0226220726.us-central1.hosted.app","availability":["RUNTIME"],"origin":"FIREBASE_SYSTEM"}]},"source":{"codebase":{"branch":"main","displayName":"1efad1f72730763da0fc1e0e9467261372f56098","hash":"1efad1f72730763da0fc1e0e9467261372f56098","commitMessage":"Analytics \"Refresh\" button now pulls live platform metrics on demand\n\nThe Analytics page read only precomputed Firestore data, and post\ninsights were captured solely on the background poller's decaying\nschedule (1h→30d), so clicking Refresh never fetched anything new —\nand posts older than 30d were frozen. This adds an on-demand path:\n\n- refreshPostsNow(workspaceId, nowIso, {productId?, channel?}) in the\n  metrics poller fetches fresh metrics for the most recent published\n  posts (bounded, light concurrency), scoped to the current\n  product/channel filter. It refreshes the denormalized\n  metricsByChannel + a stage snapshot but deliberately does NOT touch\n  the decaying schedule (metricsPollStage/metricsNextPollAt/\n  metricsStatus), so ad-hoc refreshes never rush the background\n  cadence. The per-post channel fetch loop is extracted into a shared\n  fetchPostChannelMetrics helper reused by the scheduled poller.\n- POST /api/analytics/refresh: authed (dashboard.read), rate-limited\n  per user (10/min), runs refreshPostsNow then recomputeDailyAggregates\n  on the affected UTC dates so the aggregate (all-products) view\n  reflects the new numbers too.\n- Analytics page Refresh button now calls the endpoint (\"Pulling live\n  data…\"), then re-reads analytics, with toast feedback and a 429\n  guard.\n\nTests cover the schedule-preservation invariant and channel filtering.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","uri":"https://github.com/D3vBaba/Markaestro/commit/1efad1f72730763da0fc1e0e9467261372f56098","author":{"displayName":"Rodney Sama-Ambe","email":"rodneysa@aethossolutions.com"},"commitTime":"2026-07-09T16:54:32Z"}},"buildLogsUri":"https://cons