"variable":"NG_ALLOWED_HOSTS","value":"markaestro-227206788749.us-central1.run.app,markaestro-auwks5pljq-uc.a.run.app,t-191919347---markaestro-auwks5pljq-uc.a.run.app,markaestro--markaestro-0226220726.us-central1.hosted.app","availability":["RUNTIME"],"origin":"FIREBASE_SYSTEM"}]},"source":{"codebase":{"branch":"main","displayName":"4fe17e93029b1c6b96c4639626b9ac908c42e69b","hash":"4fe17e93029b1c6b96c4639626b9ac908c42e69b","commitMessage":"fix(domains): propagate public host via x-mk-host across hosting-proxy\n\nThe host split silently no-opped in prod: the Firebase Hosting reverse\nproxy forwarded req.headers.host (the internal *.run.app name) as\nx-forwarded-host, and Google Front End rewrites x-forwarded-host to the\n*.hosted.app name on the proxy->backend hop. The Next app therefore never\nsaw app.markaestro.com / markaestro.com and every hostRedirect() bailed.\n\n- hosting-proxy: resolve the real public host from the incoming\n  x-forwarded-host (set by Firebase Hosting) and forward it as x-mk-host\n  (a non-forwarded header GFE leaves intact) plus a corrected\n  x-forwarded-host.\n- proxy.ts / robots.ts: read x-mk-host first when determining the host.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","uri":"https://github.com/D3vBaba/Markaestro/commit/4fe17e93029b1c6b96c4639626b9ac908c42e69b","author":{"displayName":"Rodney Sama-Ambe","email":"rodneysa@aethossolutions.com"},"commitTime":"2026-06-13T17:35:45Z"}},"buildLogsUri":"https://console.cloud.google.com/cloud-build/builds;region=us-central1/12935eba-e44d-4879-9d0f-409f3448c582?project=227206788749","createTime":"2026-06-13T17:35:47.848308693Z","updateTime":"2026-06-13T17:40:31.260195Z","displayName":"build-2026-06-13-002","uid":"6a987878-2fdd-4a8b-bc51-9868381aa1a7","etag":"X-vfovxjB--DU86A7sVoWB_2pU_QHJQo-1Ze4N9duWY","reconciling":false},{"name":"projects/markaestro-0226220726/locations/us-central1/backends/markaestro/builds/build-2026-03-31-002","state":"FAILED","error":{"code":1