"227206788749\",\"projectId\":\"markaestro-0226220726\",\"storageBucket\":\"markaestro-0226220726.firebasestorage.app\"}","availability":["BUILD"],"origin":"FIREBASE_SYSTEM"},{"variable":"NG_TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS","value":"X-Forwarded-Host","availability":["RUNTIME"],"origin":"FIREBASE_SYSTEM"},{"variable":"NG_ALLOWED_HOSTS","value":"markaestro-227206788749.us-central1.run.app,markaestro-auwks5pljq-uc.a.run.app,t-2366207901---markaestro-auwks5pljq-uc.a.run.app,markaestro--markaestro-0226220726.us-central1.hosted.app","availability":["RUNTIME"],"origin":"FIREBASE_SYSTEM"}]},"source":{"codebase":{"branch":"main","displayName":"5f1b754985dc16578c025e6c59e392afe5329328","hash":"5f1b754985dc16578c025e6c59e392afe5329328","commitMessage":"fix(proxy): never host-redirect /robots.txt\n\nf3199c2 put /robots.txt in MARKETING_PATHS to stop the apex bouncing it to\nthe app host. That fixed the apex but broke the other direction: the app\nhost then redirected its own /robots.txt to the apex, so a crawler fetching\napp.markaestro.com/robots.txt followed it and applied \"Allow: /\" to the\nprivate app subdomain.\n\nrobots.txt is per-host by definition and robots.ts already branches on host,\nso the request must not be relocated in either direction. Adds a\nNEVER_RELOCATED_PATHS guard alongside the existing /api/ and /_next skips.\n\n/sitemap.xml and /llms.txt stay in MARKETING_PATHS — those genuinely have a\nsingle canonical copy on the apex, and the app host redirecting to it is\ncorrect.\n\nVerified against a local server with the split flag on:\n  markaestro.com/robots.txt      200, Allow: / + app-path disallows\n  app.markaestro.com/robots.txt  200, Disallow: /   (no redirect)\n  app.markaestro.com/developers/agents  307 -> apex\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F762Pk8pUwVRx68P3doiNN","uri":"https://github.com/D3vBaba/Markaestro/commit/5f1b754985dc16578c025e6c59e392afe5329328","author":{"displa