BASE_SYSTEM"},{"variable":"NG_ALLOWED_HOSTS","value":"markaestro-227206788749.us-central1.run.app,markaestro-auwks5pljq-uc.a.run.app,t-2382985482---markaestro-auwks5pljq-uc.a.run.app,markaestro--markaestro-0226220726.us-central1.hosted.app","availability":["RUNTIME"],"origin":"FIREBASE_SYSTEM"}]},"source":{"codebase":{"branch":"main","displayName":"9fbf143c9f0ad10343790310e80e1f73c9f9c861","hash":"9fbf143c9f0ad10343790310e80e1f73c9f9c861","commitMessage":"fix(publish): resolve every destination id form and fall back instead of failing\n\nScheduled Facebook posts started failing with \"The selected facebook\naccount is no longer linked or is disconnected\" while the connections\nwere healthy.\n\nDestination ids exist in more than one shape. The public API mints\n`${provider}:${channel}:${accountId}` — `meta:facebook:1170440189496690` —\nwhile connections are keyed by the bare account id, and matching only\nknew how to strip LinkedIn's `linkedin:linkedin:` prefix. Every post\ncarrying a public-API destination id therefore matched nothing.\n\nnormalizeDestinationId now reduces the public form to its account id,\nguarding on the provider and channel segments so a LinkedIn URN\n(`urn:li:organization:99`) is never mistaken for it.\n\nThat mismatch was only fatal because an unresolvable destination returned\nnull. Refusing to publish was the wrong trade: a post must still go out\non the account the brand has connected when its recorded destination no\nlonger resolves — because the account was unlinked and relinked, or\nbecause the id predates the current format. Resolution now falls back to\nthe brand's connected account and logs the substitution\n(connections.destination.fallback) so the drift stays visible. Publishing\nonly fails when the brand has no connected account for the channel at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","uri":"https://github.com/D3vBaba/Markaestro/commit/9fbf143c9f0ad10343790310e80e1f73c9f9c861","author":{"displ