88749\",\"projectId\":\"markaestro-0226220726\",\"storageBucket\":\"markaestro-0226220726.firebasestorage.app\"}","availability":["BUILD"],"origin":"FIREBASE_SYSTEM"},{"variable":"NG_TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS","value":"X-Forwarded-Host","availability":["RUNTIME"],"origin":"FIREBASE_SYSTEM"},{"variable":"NG_ALLOWED_HOSTS","value":"markaestro-227206788749.us-central1.run.app,markaestro-auwks5pljq-uc.a.run.app,t-2745869175---markaestro-auwks5pljq-uc.a.run.app,markaestro--markaestro-0226220726.us-central1.hosted.app","availability":["RUNTIME"],"origin":"FIREBASE_SYSTEM"}]},"source":{"codebase":{"branch":"main","displayName":"0aa07f82536946583efae34b8158a0172fae7e82","hash":"0aa07f82536946583efae34b8158a0172fae7e82","commitMessage":"perf(publish): stop making the composer wait on the platform\n\nPosting held the user on a spinner for the whole round trip — three\nserial API calls plus however long Instagram took to process the media.\n\n- Drop the redundant PUT: a just-created post already holds that exact\n  payload, so only an existing draft needs its edits written back.\n- Reset the composer as soon as the post is persisted and hand the user\n  a \"Posting…\" toast, instead of blocking until the platform answers.\n  The post carries its own publishing → published/failed state in the\n  list, so a late failure is still visible.\n- Ramp the Instagram container poll (300ms, doubling to the old\n  interval) rather than sleeping a flat 2s. An image container is\n  usually ready immediately; the old poll charged ~2s of dead wait for\n  it. Same total budget, so slow video containers keep their window.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","uri":"https://github.com/D3vBaba/Markaestro/commit/0aa07f82536946583efae34b8158a0172fae7e82","author":{"displayName":"Rodney Sama-Ambe","email":"rodneysa@aethossolutions.com"},"commitTime":"2026-08-12T02:33:02Z"}},"buildLogsUri":"https://console.cloud.google.com/cloud-build/builds;region=us-central1/d32f97e2-2ca8-4643-aa55